    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 39 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners` into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, replacing the three separate telephone/email/household checks.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced the three duplicate checks (`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`, `DuplicateOwnerEmailException`, `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`) with one identity-key collision check:\n   - Compute `householdId` up front (deterministic hash, only when `sharesHousehold` is set) so it can feed the key.\n   - Build `identityKey` and reject with 409 (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`) only when a new owner's *whole* key equals an existing owner's.\n   - Kept the household-backfill logic (household members still share a `householdId`), now run only after the collision check passes.\n   - Added a private `identityKey(telephone, email, householdId)` helper.\n\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException.java`** (new) + handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 maps to 409 Conflict with an `identityKey` error field.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema (so it's returned in responses).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `identityKey(owner)` derivation mapping the returned field with the same formula.\n\n**Behavioural effect:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed (verified by `Cp11`); only an exact full-key match is a duplicate (`Cp03`, `Cp10`, `Cp25`, `Cp28`).\n\nThe three old exception classes/handlers remain but are no longer thrown \u2014 harmless dead code I left in place; say the word if you'd like them removed.",
